# Hermes Agency — Cursor Rules

Hermes Agency is the primary product in this repository. It is a Hermes Agent plugin and local operations layer for running a managed multi-agent team: packaged specialist profiles, skill-based routing, Kanban-backed work tracking, model-set controls, orchestration helpers, GPT escalation, Discord intake, and P2P delegation.

The AgentAnycast SDK under `src/agentanycast/` is the underlying transport layer. Do not present this repository as primarily an AgentAnycast SDK repo.

## Code Style

- Python 3.11+ (ruff target: py311, mypy python_version: 3.11)
- Line length: 100
- Linting: `ruff check .` (rules: E, F, I, N, W, UP)
- Formatting: `ruff format .`
- Type checking: `mypy src/` (strict mode, generated stubs excluded)
- Testing: `pytest` with `asyncio_mode = "auto"`
- Integration tests: marked `@pytest.mark.integration` (skipped by default)

## Build & Test

```bash
pip install -e ".[dev]"
ruff check .
ruff format --check .
make test-agency
make test-sdk
python -m pytest
python -m pip check
```

## Safety Rules

- All SDK/transport imports must stay lazy so Hermes can load the plugin when `agentanycast` is not installed.
- Remote task execution defaults to disabled: `allow_remote_tasks: false`.
- Incoming remote-task tools should default to `safe`, not `full`.
- Never expose API keys, tokens, private relay addresses, real peer IDs, private hostnames, or maintainer-local details in docs, tests, or fixtures.
- Management endpoints and local services should be loopback-only unless explicit remote/LAN mode is configured.

## Key Paths

- `hermes-agency/` — main product area (plugin, CLI, tools, config, staff, tests)
- `hermes-agency/default_staff/` — packaged `agency-*` staff profiles
- `hermes-agency/model_sets/` — packaged model-set strategies
- `hermes-agency/pool/` — pool-based staff setup, roster, wake/sleep, delegation
- `src/agentanycast/` — P2P transport SDK (touch only for transport tasks)
- `apps/fabric/` — Hermes Fabric frontend (separate product, see apps/fabric/README.md)
- `docker/` — headless setup/node runtime
- `tests/` — SDK unit tests
- `hermes-agency/tests/` — plugin unit tests
